🚀 Understanding Kubernetes Workloads: Job vs. InitContainer vs. Sidecar Container

Kubernetes offers powerful ways to manage workloads efficiently. Here's a simple breakdown with real-life analogies:

✅ Job → Runs once and stops (One-Time Task, Like a Delivery Boy).

✅ InitContainer → Prepares before the main app starts (Preparation Task, Like Setting Up a Restaurant Before Opening).

✅ Sidecar Container → Runs alongside the main app for extra functionality (like a DJ playing music at a party).

These concepts help in designing scalable, reliable, and efficient applications in Kubernetes.
